.Martin. wrote:
>
> 1. What am I supposed to do with a surplus of weapon/armour?

Inventory management is an important skill to learn in the first few
years of play.  On the one hand you'll gradually learn that items have
unexpected uses so more of them are useful than you think.  On the other
hand the game just keeps giving you item after item and it gets
overwhelming.  You can go from Unburdened to Burdened to Stressed to
Strained to Overtaxed by picking up items with insufficient regard to
their use.  You can even pick up enough items to fill all your inventory
letters so you can't pick up more.

I'm a pack rat.  As I explore a level I pick up items.  If one pushes me
to Burdened I will  drop my guesses at my lightest items until I am not
Burdened then take the rest to the down stairs.  I eventually shuttle
all items but rocks by the time I've explored a level.  Then I consider
what stashes are where and what should follow me and what should not. 
But even shuttling items on levels I have already explored and cleared I
do not go past Burdened and I am quick to drop enough items to be
Unburdened to fight any monster not popcorn.

Armor items are numerous but it's varying degrees of easy to tell which
ones are cursed.  Once you know that try each on.  There's no need to
carry an armor item unless you're wearing it or shuttling it to a stash
until you can see if its safe to try on.  What armor you wear will
evolve across the game as better pieces come available, the rest goes to
a stash.  Don't carry it.

Weapons items are also numoerous but far fewer of them are worth
carrying.  Even though weapons are more expendable than armor items, the
number of types that get used is more restrictive.  Chose what types of
weapons you won't ignore and what types you'll settle for until the
acceptable types start arriving, and the types you will ultimately end
up with.  No other weapon type is worth more than shuttling to your
stash.

> Shall I just drop some daggers that I don't use?

Depending on your class daggers my be at or near the top of the list of
weapon types to carry.  Even for classes that can never get past Basic
in dagger I'll gather orcish daggers until I have a "dozen", then one by
one replace them with regular daggers until they are all replaced, then
one by one replace them with elven daggers until they are all replaced,
then highly enchant the stack.  Getting any silver daggers at all is a
late game bonus.

> 2. How do you search for hidden doors ('s')? I've read that constantly
> tapping on the 's' key is discouraged from. Someone recommended
> eg. 'n10s' which will search 10x. Now my question is wether it'll search
> ten times in the square I'm standing now or will it search as I move on
> to some other places. In other words, is that command placed in one unit
> of time /one turn or it uses up 10 turns / units of time? I hope you'll
> understand what I mean.

That will search up to 10 times in the current location.  Typing s often
as you explore is a good idea but it ocsts time and therefore costs
nutrition.  How often to search is a trade off and a learned skill.


